# Duet firmware files that a separately published build replaces.
#
# One line per file:
#
#   <file> sha256:<checksum of the published build> <https location>
#
# The file has to be one the reprapfirmware package delivers below
# /opt/dsf/sd/firmware, because that is the name RepRapFirmware derives from
# the board type when it flashes; a build under any other name is never used.
# Only a published build is taken, checked against the pin: no local path, no
# fallback, a mismatch stops the build. See "Replacing a Duet firmware file"
# in the README, in particular why the build needs a version string of its
# own before any board is flashed with it.
#
# Example:
#   Duet3Firmware_TOOL1LC.bin sha256:0123...cdef https://github.com/Meltingplot/RepRapFirmware/releases/download/v3.7.0-rc.1+mp1/Duet3Firmware_TOOL1LC.bin
Duet3Firmware_TOOL1LC.bin sha256:da453b2a75571c7b23e77f2377f5ba7acdcfb8ed04e5a50814ac48f2b3e40965 https://github.com/Meltingplot/Duet3Expansion/releases/download/3.7.0%2B1.mp.2/Duet3Firmware_TOOL1LC.bin
Duet3Firmware_EXP1HCL.bin sha256:6b1ddd9e6dc284a037fb9cbe3ed5a185002a5ce9402e602b037643e89bfea25e https://github.com/Meltingplot/Duet3Expansion/releases/download/3.7.0%2B1.mp.2/Duet3Firmware_EXP1HCL.bin
Duet3Firmware_SZP.bin sha256:0e06b656eb94948486f1dfdf472ed3074e9178fbae9083890749ffa6767f6393 https://github.com/Meltingplot/Duet3Expansion/releases/download/3.7.0%2B1.mp.2/Duet3Firmware_SZP.bin
# Mainboard: RepRapFirmware 3.7-dev at upstream 3.7.0+1 (3079393dc), built by
# us against the Meltingplot library forks with a version string of its own,
# so DuetControlServer flashes it on an image update. The firmware reports its
# accelerometers under sensors.accelerometers, where DuetSoftwareFramework
# 3.7.0-rc.2 and later look for them; 3.7.0-rc.1 does not. Since 3.7.0 it
# loads the MB6HC's IAP image at 0x20458000 again, where the packaged
# Duet3_SBCiap32_MB6HC.bin is linked, and carries our fixes for macro and file
# requests over the SBC. Our CoreN2G discards the instructions the SAME70
# fetches from flash while reading the user signature, which made an MB6HC on
# 3.7.0-rc.2+1-mp.3 hard-fault in M122. On top of upstream, the main task
# carries out G-code requests from other tasks, and losing an established SBC
# connection is an emergency stop, so the mainboard resets whenever
# DuetControlServer restarts or the Pi reboots and runs config.g again once
# it reconnects. Since 3.7.0+1.mp.1 every emergency stop also turns ATX power
# off, which on the CHX 350 switches the 24 V and 48 V supply (out0 in
# e-stop.g of the printer configuration). Trigger 0 fires when its
# expression cannot be evaluated, M581.1 takes an action (U) that RRF runs
# without the SBC and a confirmation time (D), and L1 locks a trigger until
# the next restart, as trigger 0 and every trigger with an action are anyway.
# The printer configuration uses none of these trigger features yet. Since
# 3.7.0+1.mp.2 the firmware writes the code replies it has queued before any
# request that DuetControlServer matches against the order of its codes, such
# as a file abort, a macro request or a message box, so none of them overtakes
# the reply of the code before it. It no longer replies to an M99 that ends a
# macro file; DuetSoftwareFramework completes that M99 itself since
# 3.7.0+mp.6 and reports it as cancelled before. The # operator on an object
# model value that is null is an error now, where it used to return null.
Duet3Firmware_MB6HC.bin sha256:0ebda1872039f5856a889e6c6dd9dedbf6acb5b5a6036e0ad01be5978f76edfc https://github.com/Meltingplot/RepRapFirmware/releases/download/3.7.0%2B1.mp.2/Duet3Firmware_MB6HC.bin
